+# Travel Facts Integration v1 — starting reality and ownership
+
+VERIFIED: main HEAD 5572849209c943c5f5ad1579db4cef0ba2fb5b25 with extensive pre-existing dirty work. Knowledge coverage modifications are present, not deployed. Starting application hashes/status and full implementation diff retained in backend/evals/results/travel_facts_integration. Foundation 5f9f5e5 adds exactly 24 paths; all absent in main before import. Imported bytes from that commit only, without merge, cherry-pick, index changes or snapshot parent. No conflicts in external_facts/config/dependencies/database/Companion: commit changes none of these.
+
+VERIFIED: Foundation's weather contract has temperature Celsius, precipitation probability percent and WMO weather code. WeatherForecastAdapter normalizes one hourly slot and explicitly rejects current-weather capability. ResolvedFact preserves requirement, evidence, selected/rejected/conflicting facts, freshness, prediction nature and aware timestamps. Product TTL must be configured at composition root. AMap POI requires known stable ID and exposes GCJ-02; automatic text entity resolution and WGS84 conversion are absent. No coordinate-system relabelling is acceptable.
+
+Ownership: external_facts.fetch_open_meteo remains the shared network transport, not verified authority. TravelFactService + per-type registered authority/freshness resolve Companion forecasts. Existing Planning raw-weather consumer stays legacy/unmigrated and cannot be read as Companion verified fact. No new competing WeatherFact contract, weather agent or persisted weather truth.
+
+Adaptation decision: use a small internal Open-Meteo/GeoNames city-geocoding dependency to obtain WGS84 and IANA timezone, since existing AMap Foundation cannot reliably derive either from free text. Normalize its place location with existing FactRequirement/LocationValue/ResolvedFact and explicit provider registration. Only selected exact city matches allowed, no first fuzzy candidate. Bare district ambiguity needs clarification. Hangzhou West Lake is a declared city-weather alias, never exact POI identity; final answer must disclose representative city scope. No hardcoded coordinates.
+
+Reference: [Open-Meteo geocoding API](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/geocoding-api) documents WGS84 coordinates, unique IDs and timezone; [hourly forecast API](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs) documents forecast fields. No new forecast fields are introduced.
+
+Planned product policy: supported future hourly windows only; dayparts morning 06–12, afternoon 12–18, evening 18–24, full day 00–24, end exclusive. “Today” can include remaining future whole hours, not current observation or past hours. Relative dates use resolved location timezone. Exact month/day without year refers to current local year and will not silently roll to next year. Unsupported/missing/ambiguous time clarifies or limits. Max 7 local days; hourly requirements share one per-turn/day transport payload, each resolved separately. Freshness forecast 15 min, place location 24 h, stale never published. Forecast publication/model issue timestamp is unavailable in existing transport; retrieval time must not be called model issue time.
+
+Foundation Gate must pass on current main before Companion edits. Previous isolated 492 passed is historical evidence only. Final deployment is authorized by the user after all gates, and must include both Knowledge Coverage and forecast changes. No production reset or automatic itinerary changes.
